Quick start
===============================================================================

This quick start guide sets up the {{ som | upper }} on the
{{ carrier | upper }} carrier board, with JTAG through the on-board debug
agent. The software steps, OpenOCD, U-Boot and Linux, are described in
:ref:`adsp setup`; this page covers the board specific settings.

Before you start, make sure you have everything listed in
:ref:`{{ ref }} prerequisites`.

.. esd-warning::

Hardware setup
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Disconnect all power before changing switches and jumpers, or inserting the
SoM.

.. include-template:: /solutions/reference-designs/template/adsp/som-setup.rst.jinja
   :file: {{ boards }}{{ som }}.yaml

.. include-template:: /solutions/reference-designs/template/adsp/carrier-setup.rst.jinja
   :file: {{ boards }}{{ carrier }}.yaml

See the :ref:`{{ ref }} user-guide` for the positions of all switches and
jumpers.

Software setup
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Follow :ref:`adsp setup`, with these settings:

#. Start OpenOCD with the debug agent interface and the target configuration of
   the {{ processor }}:

   .. shell:: sh

      ~/openocd
      $ sudo src/openocd -f {{ openocd_interface }} \
             -f {{ openocd_target }} \
             --search tcl/ \
             --search tcl/interface/ \
             --search tcl/target/

#. Open the serial console of the SoM at 115200 8N1.
#. Download and extract the ``{{ release }}`` release, load U-Boot with GDB,
   and boot Linux with the ``{{ dtb }}`` device tree.
#. Optionally install U-Boot to the flash and Linux to the eMMC.
